### Redis Coordination Fixes (Bug #3 - FIXED)

**Problem:** All Redis CLI commands used hardcoded `localhost:6379`, ignoring `REDIS_HOST` environment variable.

**Root Cause:** Bare `redis-cli` commands default to localhost; environment variables require explicit `-h` and `-p` flags.

**Solution:**

```bash
# ❌ WRONG - defaults to localhost (ignores REDIS_HOST env var)
redis-cli HSET "swarm:${TASK_ID}:agent:${AGENT_ID}" "status" "spawned"

# ✅ CORRECT - respects environment variables
redis-cli -h "${REDIS_HOST:-localhost}" -p "${REDIS_PORT:-6379}" \
  HSET "swarm:${TASK_ID}:agent:${AGENT_ID}" "status" "spawned"
```

**Files Modified:**
- `.claude/skills/cfn-redis-coordination/report-completion.sh` (lines 69-93)
- `.claude/skills/cfn-redis-coordination/complete-swarm.sh` (lines 56, 64, 71)
- `.claude/skills/cfn-loop-orchestration/orchestrate.sh` (lines 538+)
- `src/cli/agent-executor.ts` (line 93)

**Status:** ✅ FIXED (awaiting commit)

**Impact:** Agents can now report completion to coordinator when running in Docker network with Redis container.

### API Key Propagation (Bug #1 - FIXED)

**Problem:** Coordinator only forwarded `ANTHROPIC_*` environment variables, missing provider-specific keys (Z.ai, Kimi, OpenRouter).

**Required Environment Variables:**

```javascript
// Coordinator spawning agents (docker/coordinator/src/coordinator.js lines 277-284)
const agentEnv = [
  // Z.ai (default provider - $0.50/1M tokens)
  `ZAI_API_KEY=${process.env.ZAI_API_KEY}`,
  `ZAI_BASE_URL=${process.env.ZAI_BASE_URL}`,

  // Kimi (mid-range - $2/1M tokens)
  `KIMI_API_KEY=${process.env.KIMI_API_KEY}`,
  `KIMI_BASE_URL=${process.env.KIMI_BASE_URL}`,

  // OpenRouter (400+ models - varies)
  `OPENROUTER_API_KEY=${process.env.OPENROUTER_API_KEY}`,
  `OPENROUTER_BASE_URL=${process.env.OPENROUTER_BASE_URL}`,

  // Anthropic (premium - $15/1M tokens)
